   758	
   759	_4.2.3_ _Cancel-In-Progress._ This optimization allows developers to
   760	automatically cancel an in-progress run of a job if a new run of the
   761	same job is triggered in the meanwhile.
   762	
   763	
   764	_Measuring saved time._ To quantify the saved time, we consider all
   765	runs of workflows that use the cancel-in-progress option and that
   766	are canceled. Let the VM time of such a run be _𝑡_ _𝑐𝑎𝑛𝑐𝑒𝑙𝑒𝑑_ . Next, for
   767	each such run, we check whether another run of the same workflow
   768	starts within a 5-second interval following the cancellation of the
   769	first run. Let the time taken by the second run be _𝑡_ _𝑛𝑒𝑥𝑡_ . Finally, the
   770	time difference _𝑡_ _𝑛𝑒𝑥𝑡_ − _𝑡_ _𝑐𝑎𝑛𝑐𝑒𝑙𝑒𝑑_ between the newly triggered run
   771	and the canceled run is the saved time.
